@derSoerrn95 unfortunately, I don't think this is possible 😢 

Axios uses the `XMLHttpRequest` browser API to set the headers and make the request - this API won't allow programatic modifications to [forbidden headers](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Forbidden_header_name) such as `host`.

Because this API is provided by the browser, I wouldn't be able to change the behaviour of this without modifying each client's browser that uses your app!

You can observe this by running this javascript in your browser's console:

```
const a = new XMLHttpRequest(1,2)
a.open('GET','google.com')

// doesn't set the header, throws an error because it's a forbidden header
a.setRequestHeader('host', 'yo')
a.setRequestHeader('Host', 'yo')

// allows the header to be set because it's not a forbidden header
a.setRequestHeader('abcd', 'yo')
```

