@lobatolais 
> Why this? What is causing the Jest tests to fail when updating to these new versions of axios? Also, thank you for your answer! It helped me a lot :)

To my understanding, it is because the module type of Axios at the root index file doesn't play nice with Jest, which wants a different type (CommonJS module, I believe?). The moduleNameMapper points package names to a different location, and in this case, the file I found in the distribution seems to work ok.

Just add

 "jest": {
    "transformIgnorePatterns": [
      "/node_modules/(?!(axios)/)"
    ]
  }

in package.json
and run npm install again works very well.

Anyone who faced this problem and have tried `transformIgnorePatterns` but does not work like me, please try use `moduleNameMapper` instead referring to this answer: https://stackoverflow.com/a/74297004/12733140
```
  "jest": {
    "moduleNameMapper": {
      "^axios$": "axios/dist/node/axios.cjs"
    }
  },
```

> "jest": {
>     "moduleNameMapper": {
>       "^axios$": "axios/dist/node/axios.cjs"
>     }
>   },

This is the only solution which worked for me! Thanks @hacker0limbo :)

